Kitten ASR inference engine (in the kitten-inference package)
Copyright 2026 KittenML

The engine (src/kitten_inference/asr/ in this repository, installed as
kitten_inference/asr/) is KittenML code, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (LICENSE), except that the parts listed below follow or are
adapted from other projects. It runs speech-to-text models that have an
audio encoder and a text decoder. On NVIDIA GPUs it is Python code that runs
on PyTorch. On CPUs and on the GPU of Macs it is a compiled engine
(engines/asr-cpu/ in this repository, installed as
kitten_inference/_asr_cpu/), described under "The CPU engine" below.

Code that follows other projects
--------------------------------
- Attention kernels. The Triton attention kernels in
  kitten_inference/asr/_attn.py (prefill, decode in one pass, and decode with
  the keys cut into pieces plus the step that merges the pieces) follow the
  structure of the Triton attention kernels in SGLang, whose decode kernel
  also works in two stages:
    https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang
    Apache License, Version 2.0. Copyright 2023-2024 SGLang Team.
  SGLang's decode kernel is adapted from LightLLM:
    https://github.com/ModelTC/lightllm
    Apache License, Version 2.0.
  The kernels also follow the fused-attention tutorial of Triton:
    https://github.com/triton-lang/triton
    MIT License (https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/blob/main/LICENSE).
  The text of the Apache License, Version 2.0 is in LICENSE.

- Low-precision matrix product. The Triton kernel in
  kitten_inference/asr/_quant.py (8-bit and 4-bit integer weights, 8-bit
  float weights and activations) follows the tiling of the matrix
  multiplication tutorial of Triton (grouped program order, float32
  accumulation):
    https://github.com/triton-lang/triton
    MIT License (https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/blob/main/LICENSE).

- Mel filter bank. _mel_filters in kitten_inference/asr/_loader.py, the
  Slaney-scale mel filter bank, is adapted from
  transformers.audio_utils.mel_filter_bank of Hugging Face Transformers:
    https://github.com/huggingface/transformers
    Apache License, Version 2.0. Copyright 2023 The HuggingFace Inc. team
    and the librosa & torchaudio authors.

- Encoder position table. _sinusoid in kitten_inference/asr/_loader.py, the
  sinusoidal position table of the audio encoder, uses the formula of the
  `sinusoids` function in OpenAI Whisper:
    https://github.com/openai/whisper
    MIT License (https://github.com/openai/whisper/blob/main/LICENSE).
    Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI.

