The model converter (kitten_inference/asr/_gguf.py) writes the GGUF file
format of ggml with NumPy; it is KittenML code and contains no llama.cpp code.

Not included
------------
- Model weights. On first use the package downloads them from Hugging Face
  (KittenML/kitten-asr-tiny, KittenML/kitten-asr-small-enhanced, or the model
  you name). They keep the license shown on their Hugging Face pages.
- PyTorch, which you install separately (pip install torch) under its own
  license (needed for NVIDIA GPUs only), and the Triton compiler that the package's own attention kernels
  are compiled with when they are used.
- The runtime dependencies of kitten-inference (among them NumPy,
  huggingface-hub, SoundFile and tokenizers), which pip installs separately
  under their own licenses.
